<title>CHINA: ITC HOLDINGS YEAR NET RISES 125.6 PCT.</title>
<headline>ITC HOLDINGS YEAR NET RISES 125.6 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 57.1	 vs 26.3</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  6.0	  vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	55.01 gain vs 11.85 gain</p>
<p>    Net			  162.88     vs 72.20</p>
<p>    Turnover		   282.93     vs 320.89</p>
<p>    Company name	     International Tak Cheung Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		September 22-26</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 October 31</p>
<p>NOTE - International Tak Cheung is a civil engineering firm and concrete products maker.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$97.15 million on disposals of subsidiaries and associated companies, gain of HK$4.32 million on write back for properties held for resale and HK$46.46 million loss on investments.</p>
<p>Total dividend of year is eight H.K. cents (including interim dividend of two cents) vs three cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
